{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
From Jeconiah’s line [Dm]in the captives' [C]land
Shealtiel his [Bb]son, holding the [Dm]hand
Of Malchiram, Pedaiah, and Shenaz[C]zar
Jekamiah, Hos[Bb]hama, and Nedabi[Dm]ah
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
From Pedaiah’s house, Zerubbabel [C]rose
With Shimei his [Bb]brother, the line is [Dm]closed
Meshullam and Hananiah, sons of the [C]king
And Shelomith [Bb]their sister, the bond [Dm]is strong
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Hananiah, name in the royal ge[C]nealogy
Son of Ze[Bb]rubbabel, part of [Dm]the lineage
David’s blood flows on, through the exile’s [C]night
The line of Ju[Bb]dah, burning with [Dm]light
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
The sons of Hananiah, Pelatiah and [C]Jeshaiah
Continuing the [Bb]path, the truth is [Dm]laid
Through Rephaiah, Arnan, and Obadi[C]ah
Shecaniah’s sons, [Bb]in the books dis[Dm]played
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Hananiah, name in the royal ge[C]nealogy
Son of Ze[Bb]rubbabel, part of [Dm]the lineage
David’s blood flows on, through the exi[C]le’s night
The line of [Bb]Judah, burning with [Dm]light
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
No [Bb]throne is built in the city [Dm]stone
But [Bb]names are kept in the book a[Dm]lone
The house of Da[Bb]vid, preserved and [Dm]true
In Chronicles’ pa[Bb]ges, writ[C]ten for [Dm]you
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
The line con[Bb]tinues, the sto[Dm]ry stands
Hanani[Bb]ah’s name, in [C]the promised [Dm]lands
